/jasoaco79/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasoaco79/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasoaco79/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasoaco79/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasoaco79","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jasoaco79/demo-injector/commits/7aefdf5c4b67b38c70f5489ec9f37966c198d409/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-24T01:12:21Z","email":"jasoaco79@users.noreply.github.com","name":"jasoaco79"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-24T01:12:21Z","email":"jasoaco79@users.noreply.github.com","name":"jasoaco79"},"message":"Add device list interceptors + catch-all debug logging\n\n- Added catch-all patterns for device/endpoint list APIs\n  (various URL patterns the devices page might use)\n- Added debug logging for unhandled Sophos API calls\n  Shows [Sophos Demo] 🔍 Unhandled: in console for any API\n  we intercept but don''t modify — helps identify missing endpoints\n- Saved devices-capture data\n- Preserved deep-capture-full.json (57 endpoints from auto-capture)\n\nThe Devices → Computers page uses a micro-frontend that loads\ndevice lists through an unknown API pattern. Debug logging will\nreveal the exact endpoint when tested with demo mode ON.","tree":{"sha":"33862098f190b1a2b89040b57faf11dac22c6eb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jasoaco79/demo-injector/git/trees/33862098f190b1a2b89040b57faf11dac22c6eb4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jasoaco79/demo-injector/git/commits/7aefdf5c4b67b38c70f5489ec9f37966c198d409","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260302728?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasoaco79/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasoaco79/followers","following_url":"https://