lashpoint/commits/a2f8d300624eadd6ad57ca1899c0caba9d8dfc40/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-25T05:06:51Z","email":"axelbaumcharles@gmail.com","name":"Charlie Axelbaum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-25T05:06:51Z","email":"axelbaumcharles@gmail.com","name":"Charlie Axelbaum"},"message":"feat(ui): surface last-known-data fallback with SERVED FROM CACHE badge\n\nDesktop PRD \\xc2\\xa726: ''show last known data on feed failure.''\n\nVerification: the existing 60s poll''s .catch never overwrites hotspots/\npriorities/systemStatus, so part (a) of the contract \\xe2\\x80\\x94 keep rendering\nthe last-good snapshot \\xe2\\x80\\x94 was already satisfied. Part (b) was missing:\nthe operator had no signal that the data on screen was from a failed\nread.\n\n- App.jsx adds lastPollFailed state, set true in .catch and false in\n  .then, passed into StatusBar\n- StatusBar.jsx renders a SERVED FROM CACHE badge (stale variant) when\n  lastPollFailed is true\n- Comment in .catch makes the no-overwrite invariant load-bearing and\n  documented\n\nVerified: frontend builds clean, no new lint errors introduced (the\nsingle pre-existing App.jsx warning is unrelated).","tree":{"sha":"12bc872bd922456a29a076f5103efb87e612ed57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/git/trees/12bc872bd922456a29a076f5103efb87e612ed57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/git/commits/a2f8d300624eadd6ad57ca1899c0caba9d8dfc40","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64117841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlie-axelbaum","id":64117841,"login":"charlie-axelbaum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTE3ODQx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commit/a2f8d300624eadd6ad57ca1899c0caba9d8dfc40","node_id":"C_kwDORuGHBNoAKGEyZjhkMzAwNjI0ZWFkZDZhZDU3Y2ExODk5YzBjYWJhOWQ4ZGZjNDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commit/3169039079504c378e22f8c2ec7019a445fc9fc2","sha":"3169039079504c378e22f8c2ec7019a445fc9fc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commits/3169039079504c378e22f8c2ec7019a445fc9fc2"}],"sha":"a2f8d300624eadd6ad57ca1899c0caba9d8dfc40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commits/a2f8d300624eadd6ad57ca1899c0caba9d8dfc40"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64117841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlie-axelbaum","id":64117841,"login":"charlie-axelbaum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTE3ODQx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commits/3169039079504c378e22f8c2ec7019a445fc9fc2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-25T05:05:35Z","email":"axelbaumcharles@gmail.com","name":"Charlie Axelbaum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-25T05:05:35Z","email":"axelbaumcharles@gmail.com","name":"Charlie Axelbaum"},"message":"feat(shell): rotating file logging with backend readiness timing\n\nDesktop PRD \\xc2\\xa727 requires shell launch logs, backend readiness\ntiming, web-view load failures, and autostart diagnostics. Today\nwindow.py prints to stdout, which XDG autostart discards on Pi \\xe2\\x80\\x94\nwhen the shell fails on boot, there is no log to read.\n\nRoutes all _log() calls through a Python Logger configured with both\na RotatingFileHandler at ~/.flashpoint/shell.log (5 MB cap, 3 backups)\nand a stream handler for dev runs. Captures monotonic timing at\n_start_connecting and emits elapsed seconds in _on_backend_ready\n(''READY in 1.82s'') and _on_backend_unavailable (''UNAVAILABLE after\n20.04s''). Adds a startup line with the resolved backend and frontend\nURLs so Pi diagnostics can confirm env-var injection.\n\nVerified: importing the module creates ~/.flashpoint/, _log() writes\nthe timestamped ''shell'' line to the file, log rotates at 5 MB.","tree":{"sha":"9fb77e4f90b03700f5e5b52118a7c68ef554a289","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/git/trees/9fb77e4f90b03700f5e5b52118a7c68ef554a289"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/git/commits/3169039079504c378e22f8c2ec7019a445fc9fc2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64117841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlie-axelbaum","id":64117841,"login":"charlie-axelbaum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTE3ODQx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commit/3169039079504c378e22f8c2ec7019a445fc9fc2","node_id":"C_kwDORuGHBNoAKDMxNjkwMzkwNzk1MDRjMzc4ZTIyZjhjMmVjNzAxOWE0NDVmYzlmYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commit/b6fece936ce28be0addd0c0b580f8913c7cebede","sha":"b6fece936ce28be0addd0c0b580f8913c7cebede","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commits/b6fece936ce28be0addd0c0b580f8913c7cebede"}],"sha":"3169039079504c378e22f8c2ec7019a445fc9fc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commits/3169039079504c378e22f8c2ec7019a445fc9fc2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64117841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlie-axelbaum","id":64117841,"login":"charlie-axelbaum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTE3ODQx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commits/b6fece936ce28be0addd0c0b580f8913c7cebede/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-25T05:04:44Z","email":"axelbaumcharles@gmail.com","name":"Charlie Axelbaum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-25T05:04:44Z","email":"axelbaumcharles@gmail.com","name":"Charlie Axelbaum"},"message":"fix(db): enable SQLite WAL mode and 30s busy timeout\n\nThe launcher process, the APScheduler ingest job, and FastAPI request\nworkers all share data/flashpoint.db. SQLite''s default DELETE journal\nblocks readers during a writer transaction; under contention the\nsecond operation raises ''database is locked''. WAL mode lets readers\nproceed alongside a single writer, and timeout=30 lets the rare\nsecond writer wait for the lock instead of failing immediately.\n\n- connect_args adds timeout=30\n- New connect-event hook runs PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL and\n  synchronous=NORMAL on every connection\n- New test_database_concurrency.py asserts WAL is active and that a\n  reader on a separate connection completes while a writer holds an\n  open transaction\n\nVerified: 110 tests pass (was 108), live data/flashpoint.db reports\nPRAGMA journal_mode=wal after backend startup, with the expected\n.db-wal and .db-shm sidecar files.","tree":{"sha":"8b4a7d23111fc42c97aa16e2816851fa32dc5d02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/git/trees/8b4a7d23111fc42c97aa16e2816851fa32dc5d02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/git/commits/b6fece936ce28be0addd0c0b580f8913c7cebede","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64117841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlie-axelbaum","id":64117841,"login":"charlie-axelbaum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTE3ODQx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commit/b6fece936ce28be0addd0c0b580f8913c7cebede","node_id":"C_kwDORuGHBNoAKGI2ZmVjZTkzNmNlMjhiZTBhZGRkMGMwYjU4MGY4OTEzYzdjZWJlZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commit/20b1942f1f211447e43d67b27c9f28df7aca8f26","sha":"20b1942f1f211447e43d67b27c9f28df7aca8f26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commits/20b1942f1f211447e43d67b27c9f28df7aca8f26"}],"sha":"b6fece936ce28be0addd0c0b580f8913c7cebede","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commits/b6fece936ce28be0addd0c0b580f8913c7cebede"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64117841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlie-axelbaum","id":64117841,"login":"charlie-axelbaum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTE3ODQx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commits/20b1942f1f211447e43d67b27c9f28df7aca8f26/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-25T05:03:46Z","email":"axelbaumcharles@gmail.com","name":"Charlie Axelbaum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-25T05:03:46Z","email":"axelbaumcharles@gmail.com","name":"Charlie Axelbaum"},"message":"refactor(time): route all utcnow() through app.utils.time helpers\n\ndatetime.utcnow() is deprecated in Python 3.12+ and returns a tz-naive\ndatetime. The project utility at backend/app/utils/time.py is now the\nsingle source for current-time values.\n\nTwo helpers are exposed because the project has two distinct boundaries:\n\n  - utcnow() returns a tz-aware UTC datetime, used at API serialization\n    boundaries (health endpoint timestamp via the new to_iso_z helper)\n    and for in-process arithmetic via the new to_utc coercion helper.\n\n  - utcnow_naive() returns a naive UTC datetime, used at the database\n    boundary. Existing rows in data/flashpoint.db were written by the\n    old datetime.utcnow() (also naive); inserting tz-aware values into\n    the same naive DateTime columns would serialize with a +00:00 suffix\n    and break SQLite string-sort comparisons against legacy rows.\n\nHealth endpoint timestamp now uses to_iso_z(utcnow()) which produces a\nclean ''...T...Z'' string. system.py''s is_stale arithmetic wraps\nlast_success_at in to_utc() before subtraction so the comparison works\nwhether the DB row is naive or tz-aware.\n\nVerified: 108 backend tests pass, /api/v1/health returns 200 with a Z\ntimestamp, /api/v1/system/status computes is_stale against the live DB\nwithout TypeError.","tree":{"sha":"595746e941d05bd59d267165433c16bad51611ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/git/trees/595746e941d05bd59d267165433c16bad51611ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/git/commits/20b1942f1f211447e43d67b27c9f28df7aca8f26","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64117841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlie-axelbaum","id":64117841,"login":"charlie-axelbaum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MTE3ODQx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/received_events","repos_ur