axelbaum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commits/cbba7efddfc805718337095229c4033ffa4141a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-24T22:35:17Z","email":"axelbaumcharles@gmail.com","name":"Charlie Axelbaum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-24T22:35:17Z","email":"axelbaumcharles@gmail.com","name":"Charlie Axelbaum"},"message":"feat: improve hotspot naming precision\n\nReplace frequency-only city selection in _hotspot_name() with a\nproximity-weighted ranking: score = count / (1 + mean_dist_miles / 50).\nCities far from the cluster centroid need proportionally more event support\nto win the label — peripheral frequency cannot override geographic fit.\n\nPass the actual running-mean centroid from _cluster_events() into\n_hotspot_name() so naming stays aligned with real cluster geometry.\n\nApply the same proximity weighting to county/parish fallback.\n\nAdd backend/tests/test_hotspot_naming.py (9 unittest cases) covering\nfiltering exclusions, proximity tie-breaking, fallback chain, and\nstate-abbreviation expansion.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"40a1b6ba1a34026d56e822d75580d2bf9955cb4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/git/trees/40a1b6ba1a34026d56e822d75580d2bf9955cb4f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/git/commits/cbba7efddfc805718337095229c4033ffa4141a5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64117841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https: