/charlie-axelbaum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/commits/2c8fa549a6ba3bac76e125ee953e2401aae12ec4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-24T16:57:49Z","email":"axelbaumcharles@gmail.com","name":"Charlie Axelbaum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-24T16:57:49Z","email":"axelbaumcharles@gmail.com","name":"Charlie Axelbaum"},"message":"feat: make hotspots and priorities data-driven\n\nReplace 5 hardcoded centroid seeds with greedy radius clustering of\ningested events. Hotspots now derive from real signal density using\nhaversine distance (150-mile radius). State-level and country-level\ngeocodes are handled explicitly: they may join nearby clusters but\ncannot anchor or create fallback hotspots. Naming uses a city →\ncounty → state-region → coordinate hierarchy with full state names\nto avoid abbreviation ambiguity. Priority scores and event coverage\nnow reflect actual GDELT signal distribution.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a7931f29495918f403fb8c9d8401c158616f7972","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/git/trees/a7931f29495918f403fb8c9d8401c158616f7972"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/charlie-axelbaum/Flashpoint/git/commits/2c8fa549a6ba3bac76e125ee953e2401aae12ec4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64117841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlie-axelbaum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/