i.github.com/users/notTag/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notTag/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notTag/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/notTag/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/notTag","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/notTag/nicktagportal/commits/9e57c3ed45976a96bb6c1fe1c995f99011d3f176/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-19T23:27:48Z","email":"nick.tagliasacchi@gmail.com","name":"Nick Tagliasacchi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-19T23:27:48Z","email":"nick.tagliasacchi@gmail.com","name":"Nick Tagliasacchi"},"message":"refactor(10-06): TheSidebar standalone + drag follow + footer clearance + rail grip\n\nUAT polish + library portability, atomic across four files so the app\ntree is never in a broken state:\n\n- TheSidebar.vue accepts ''store: SidebarStore'' via prop; removes the\n  ''@/stores/sidebar'' import. Component is now portable within packages/ui\n  — no shell-app dependency leaks in.\n- AppLayout.vue instantiates useSidebarStore and passes it to TheSidebar.\n  Shell owns the store instance; library owns the rendering contract.\n- Drag visual feedback: '':style=\"dragStyle\"'' binds translateX(dragOffsetX)\n  while is-dragging. Snap resumes on release (offset resets to 0 and the\n  is-dragging class drops).\n- Footer clearance: new ''--sidebar-bottom-inset: 5rem'' token; aside binds\n  ''bottom'' to it via inline style. No more overlapping TheFooter.\n- Rail grip affordance: hamburger-style SVG in the header that''s visible\n  only when collapsed, matching the brand/close fade pattern.\n- TheSidebar.test.ts replaces its ''@/stores/sidebar'' import with a plain\n  SidebarStore mock. Adds: grip-present, drag-transform, portability\n  self-check (file-read regex for ''@/stores''). 15/15 pass.","tree":{"sha":"7c9595efab5e89424c83be28874d91026d602354","url":"http